%[text] # comp.SemiInductanceDriver Class
%[text] **J.G. Vermond, JVsound**
%[text] Loudspeaker driver with a semi-inductance in the impedance of the voice coil.
%[text] **Namespace:** comp
%[text] **Superclasses:** [comp.Driver](matlab:open(fullfile(fileparts(fileparts(which('lspsys'))),'doc','comp','driver','driverdoc.m')))
%%
%[text] ## Description
%[text] The `comp.SemiInductanceDriver` class is a [`comp.Driver`](matlab:open(fullfile(fileparts(fileparts(which('lspsys'))),'doc','comp','driver','driverdoc.m'))) with a more accurate model of the blocked electrical impedance. Besides the resistance $ R\_e $ and the inductance $ L\_e $ of the voice coil, it has the semi-inductance $ K\_e $ of the model of J. Vanderkooy:
%[text]{"align":"center"} $ Z\_{eb} = R\_e + j \\omega L\_e + K\_e \\sqrt{j \\omega} $
%[text] The last term describes the losses by eddy currents in the pole piece: at high frequencies the impedance of a real voice coil rises less than with an inductance alone, with the square root of the frequency, and its phase stays below 90°. Source: J. Vanderkooy, "A model of loudspeaker driver impedance incorporating eddy currents in the pole structure", J. Audio Eng. Soc., vol. 37, no. 3, 1989.
%[text] $ L\_e $ and $ K\_e $ must come from the same fit of the measured impedance: the inductance of a datasheet is usually fitted with $ K\_e = 0 $ and then already holds part of the effect. With `SemiInductance` set to 0, the driver is the same as `comp.Driver`.
%[text] All other parameters and methods are those of `comp.Driver`. Only `zeb` is different; `te`, and so [`lspsys`](matlab:open(fullfile(fileparts(fileparts(which('lspsys'))),'doc','lspsys','lspsysdoc.m'))), uses it. A `comp.SemiInductanceDriver` can be used everywhere a `comp.Driver` can, for example as the `Driver` of an enclosure.
%%
%[text] ## Creation
%[text] ```matlabCodeExample
%[text] obj = comp.SemiInductanceDriver
%[text] ```
%[text] Creates a driver with all parameters set to 0, as `comp.Driver` does, and `SemiInductance` set to 0. Set the parameters of the datasheet and the fit before you use the driver.
%%
%[text] ## Properties
%[text] The class adds one property. All properties of `comp.Driver` are inherited; see its page.
%%
%[text] ### `SemiInductance` — Semi-inductance of the voice coil
%[text] `(1,1) double` \[Ohm s^0.5\]
%[text] Semi-inductance $ K\_e $ of the voice coil, in $ \\Omega \\, \\mathrm{s}^{1/2} $. Must be nonnegative. Default: 0.
%[text] **Attributes:** `GetAccess = public`, `SetAccess = public`
%%
%[text] ## Methods
%[text:table]{"columnWidths":[120,100,-1]}
%[text] | Method | Type | Description |
%[text] | --- | --- | --- |
%[text] | `zeb` | Instance | Blocked electrical impedance $ Z\_{eb} = R\_e + j \\omega L\_e + K\_e \\sqrt{j \\omega} $ at frequencies `f`. Overrides [`zeb`](matlab:open(fullfile(fileparts(fileparts(which('lspsys'))),'doc','comp','driver','methods','zebdoc','zebdoc.m'))) of `comp.Driver`. |
%[text] | [`zm`](matlab:open(fullfile(fileparts(fileparts(which('lspsys'))),'doc','comp','driver','methods','zmdoc','zmdoc.m'))) | Instance | Mechanical impedance $ Z\_m $, inherited from `comp.Driver`. |
%[text] | [`te`](matlab:open(fullfile(fileparts(fileparts(which('lspsys'))),'doc','comp','driver','methods','tedoc','tedoc.m'))) | Instance | Transmission matrix $ \\mathbf{T}\_e $ of the electrical side, from `zeb`; inherited from `comp.Driver`. |
%[text] | [`tbl`](matlab:open(fullfile(fileparts(fileparts(which('lspsys'))),'doc','comp','driver','methods','tbldoc','tbldoc.m'))) | Instance | Transmission matrix $ \\mathbf{T}\_{bl} $, inherited from `comp.Driver`. |
%[text] | [`tm`](matlab:open(fullfile(fileparts(fileparts(which('lspsys'))),'doc','comp','driver','methods','tmdoc','tmdoc.m'))) | Instance | Transmission matrix $ \\mathbf{T}\_m $, inherited from `comp.Driver`. |
%[text] | [`tsd`](matlab:open(fullfile(fileparts(fileparts(which('lspsys'))),'doc','comp','driver','methods','tsddoc','tsddoc.m'))) | Instance | Transmission matrix $ \\mathbf{T}\_{sd} $, inherited from `comp.Driver`. |
%[text:table]
%%
%[text] ## Examples
%%
%[text] ### Example: Blocked impedance with a semi-inductance
%[text] Create a `comp.Driver` and a `comp.SemiInductanceDriver` with the `Re` and `Le` of the B&C 21SW152-8, and compare the magnitude of their blocked electrical impedance. The semi-inductance of 0.03 Ohm s^0.5 is a value for illustration, not a fitted value of this driver.
d = comp.Driver;
d.Re = 6;
d.Le = 2.2e-3;
s = comp.SemiInductanceDriver;
s.Re = 6;
s.Le = 2.2e-3;
s.SemiInductance = 0.03;
f = logspace(1,4,300);
semilogx(f,abs(d.zeb(f)),f,abs(s.zeb(f)),"--",LineWidth=1.5) %[output:7bd8acae]
grid on %[output:7bd8acae]
xlabel("Frequency [Hz]") %[output:7bd8acae]
ylabel("|Z_{eb}| [\Omega]") %[output:7bd8acae]
legend("comp.Driver","comp.SemiInductanceDriver",Location="northwest") %[output:7bd8acae]

